---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Program = `let names       = ["Ade","Bianca","Cyrus","Dara","Elian",
                   "Farah","Gus","Hana","Ivo","Jo"];
let grade       = [11, 11, 11, 12, 12, 11, 12, 11, 12, 11];
let homeroom    = ["B","B","C","A","A","B","A","C","A","B"];
let birthMonth  = ["Mar","Sep","Mar","Jul","Mar",
                   "Sep","Nov","Jul","Jul","Mar"];
let club        = ["Chess","Chess","Robotics","Robotics","Chess",
                   "Debate","Robotics","Debate","Chess","Robotics"];

// Publish the club sign-ups, anonymized.
function publish()
{
  console.log("grade  homeroom  birth  club");

  for (let i = 0; i < names.length; i++)
  {
    console.log(grade[i] + "     " + homeroom[i] +
                "         " + birthMonth[i] + "    " + club[i]);
  }
}

publish();`;

const Output = `grade  homeroom  birth  club
11     B         Mar    Chess
11     B         Sep    Chess
11     C         Mar    Robotics
12     A         Jul    Robotics
12     A         Mar    Chess
11     B         Sep    Debate
12     A         Nov    Robotics
11     C         Jul    Debate
12     A         Jul    Chess
11     B         Mar    Robotics`;

const TheClaim = `THE CLAIM

  "The names are removed, so the data is anonymous."

The names ARE removed. The output above contains
no name and no student number.

Test the claim.`;

const WhoKnows = `WHAT A READER MIGHT ALREADY KNOW

  Homeroom lists are posted on the wall.
  Birthdays get announced in assembly.

  So a reader may plausibly know, for any student,
  their grade, their homeroom, and their birth month.

They do not need the names list.
They need to recognize a row.`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Debug Challenge: The Anonymous Data</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">
          On paper &middot; the program is correct &middot; the claim is not
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>
            <b>A school wants to publish which clubs are popular</b> without revealing
            who joined what. Somebody wrote this, removed the names, and published the
            result.
          </p>

          <Code code={TheClaim} frame="code" lang="txt" title="The Claim" showLineNumbers={false} class="my-3" />

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">The program does exactly what it says.</b> There is
            no bug. <b>The defect is in what somebody believed the output meant.</b>
          </p>

          <p class="text-body-secondary">
            <b>Paper only.</b> You can do all of this by reading the table.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="program">
          <h2>The Program</h2>

          <Code code={Program} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="publish" class="mb-4" />

          <h3>What It Publishes</h3>

          <Code code={Output} frame="terminal" lang="txt" title="Ten Rows, No Names" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-4" />

          <Code code={WhoKnows} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Before You Start" showLineNumbers={false} />
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <h3>1. Break the Claim</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <b>Which rows are the only row with their combination of grade, homeroom
              and birth month?</b> List them.
            </li>
            <li><b>How many of the ten students are uniquely identified this way?</b></li>
            <li>
              For each one you found, <b>name the student</b> (you have the names list)
              and say <b>what has now been published about them.</b>
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Which students are safe, and why?</b> What do they have that the others
              do not?
            </li>
          </ol>

          <h3 class="mt-4">2. Name What Happened</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>
              No single published column identifies anybody. <b>What is the word for
              combining data this way to create knowledge about an individual?</b>
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Is grade PII? Is homeroom? Is birth month?</b> Answer for each, then
              answer for all three together.
            </li>
            <li>
              The definition of PII has four verbs. <b>Which one applies to a birth
              month?</b>
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Is there a syntax error? A logic error?</b> Does <code>publish</code>{" "}
              do what its name says?
            </li>
          </ol>

          <h3 class="mt-4">3. Fix It</h3>

          <p><b>Four options. Work out what each actually achieves.</b></p>

          <table class="table table-sm align-middle mt-3">
            <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>How many students remain uniquely identified?</th><th>What is lost</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><b>A.</b> Also remove <code>birthMonth</code></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td><b>B.</b> Also remove <code>homeroom</code>, keep birth month</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td><b>C.</b> Publish only the totals per club, no rows at all</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td><b>D.</b> Publish rows only where at least three students share the combination</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <ol>
            <li><b>Work out the numbers for A and B by hand.</b> One of them fixes it completely.</li>
            <li><b>Which option would you choose, and what does the school lose?</b></li>
            <li>
              <b>Option C loses the most and is the safest.</b> Say what question the
              school can no longer answer with it.
            </li>
          </ol>

          <h3 class="mt-4">4. The General Lesson</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <b>Write one sentence</b> that a person publishing any dataset should check
              before they publish it.
            </li>
            <li>
              At session 43 you removed the location from a photo's metadata and the
              image was unchanged. <b>Explain how that activity and this one are the same
              idea from opposite directions.</b>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            All four sections, including your completed options table with the numbers
            worked out for A and B.
          </p>

          <p>Worth <b>4 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
